description:
Replaces WT-19a (task-5ac436aa967740d89c440d0f6f120547, archived). That row's DoD assumed main as the target and a post-WT-10M snapshot. On 11-02 the human decided "keep main PR-only, land on a branch". This project therefore switches to worktree mode with consolidationBranch 'moe/work-2026-10-24'. It does not run the migration landing, so WT-10M is no longer a prerequisite of the switch. This row is split from WT-19 (task-b1ca54f2716442be889a14623eb59983) DoD 5; its shape is architect-0fcb7226's #architects msg-27859513, adapted to that decision. The human's go on the early switch is #general msg-717a48e0.

Goal: before this project switches, prove three things on the post-WT-13 wrapper bytes, in the production shape (a slash-named, non-main target with main left alone):
- two parallel tasks and one conflict-resumed task land on the target with fast-forward-only history;
- the control checkout follows;
- the candidate qualityGate passes in the sparse gate worktree.
If the run fails, the switch waits.

One new file: scripts/tests/worktree-e2e.cjs, modelled on postflight-worktree.cjs.
- It keeps WT-19 step 2's CLI: `<sh|ps1> <wrapper> <fake-proxy> <parent-tmp> <engine>`.
- It runs the real wrappers against the shared fake proxy, with no real daemon.
- Fixture under <parent-tmp>:
  - a `git init` repo whose first commit is this repo's HEAD tree, so the gate's scripts exist;
  - a local bare origin;
  - a `main` branch;
  - a slash-named target branch, e.g. moe/work-e2e, cut from main;
  - the control checkout on moe/control, created at the target's tip;
  - settings: worktreeMode 'on', consolidationBranch set to the target, qualityGate set to the candidate `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && npm run lint`.
- Scenarios: (a) parallel and (b) conflict-resume, as WT-19 step 2 defines them, landing on the target.
- The slash in the target also exercises the target-name paths: the land-lease id sanitizer, the L10 mirror, the control follow and the checked-out-target check.

WT-19 step 2 already planned this file under the same name and CLI, and WT-19's step 6 gate line runs it. WT-19 extends it later with its main-target and ps1 legs.

Dependency: WT-13 (task-fbe8e3880ddf47dfa8546f220acea770). Its chain WT-13 → WT-12 → WT-11 → WT-10 puts the LANDING-CONFLICT resume and the control follow on HEAD before this row can be claimed. postflight-fake-proxy.js and postflight-worktree.cjs are lane files, so this row edits no existing file.

NOT in scope:
- any edit to an existing file;
- this repo's main, moe/control, settings or GitHub origin;
- the ps1 engine leg and scenario (c), the remote race. Both stay with WT-19.

Verification: `node scripts/tests/worktree-e2e.cjs sh scripts/moe-agent.sh scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js "$(mktemp -d -p /mnt/d/moe-scratch wt-e2e.XXXXXX)" "$(command -v bash)"`. Widen MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC if drvfs is slow.

implementationPlan.note:
Scenario (a) `parallel()` plus the shared checks. Seats a and b are spawned together and awaited together. a writes e2e/a.txt and edits shared.txt line 2; b writes e2e/b.txt and edits line 8.
Assertions:
- both exit 0, no report_blocked, each logs `[worktree] created <W> on moe/task/task-<s>`, and no .moe (lstat) in either W;
- exactly +2 commits; linear() checks no merges since the fixture tip, every reflog entry a fast-forward of the one before, origin's target == local, and main unchanged locally and in origin;
- the target's tree holds a.txt, b.txt and the two-hunk shared.txt;
- each seat's single finalize_attempt is 'landed' on one of the two new commits, with a committed completion record_commit;
- the interposer's lease holds are one per task and disjoint.
afterLanding(runs, g0), in order:
- `[OK] qualityGate passed.` per landing session;
- gate-runs.log lines since g0 == the logged "Post-flight: quality gate:" count, each a <tmp>/moe-gate.*/tree path that is neither the control nor any W;
- no MOE_CONTROL_NOT_FOLLOWING, CHECKOUT_BEHIND or CHECKOUT_DIVERGED in any log;
- MOE_CONTROL_ADVANCED per landing session;
- control on refs/heads/moe/control, HEAD == the target, porcelain clean.
Trial 2 (HEAD 241ac770 snapshot, no verification) passed everything up to MOE_CONTROL_ADVANCED, the expected pre-WT-13 failure. Both landed through the lease and the gate in about 73 s. With the two WT-13 follow assertions removed in a /tmp scratch copy only, parallel printed ok (72.7 s).
Code spellings come from the plan and design §6, because WT-13 has not landed; the resume session greps WT-13's landed wrapper first, and the code wins.

implementationPlan.description:
Scenario (b) `conflict-resume`. It needs (a) to pass; otherwise print FAILED 'needs parallel', never SKIP.

Session c1 (task-c, worker-e2e-c). The CLI writes e2e/c.txt and shared.txt line 2 as `line 2: task-c`, which conflicts with task-a's landed line 2. task-c's branch was cut before (a). Assert:
- the log has MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_CONFLICT;
- the target sha is unchanged and main is unchanged;
- seat c's rpcs show finalize_attempt outcome 'unlanded' with unlandedReason 'conflict', conflictPaths containing e2e/shared.txt, and a rescueRef under refs/moe/rescue/task-c/ that resolves to moe/task/task-c's tip;
- there is a failed completion record_commit with that code, and no 'landed' finalize.

Between sessions: delete seat c's fake attempts/ and context-count so the next claim opens a new attempt (session 2's ids). Keep the stored landingRetry.

Session c2: E2E_CLI_EXPECT_MARKERS=e2e/shared.txt, and the CLI writes the resolved shared.txt (line 2 `line 2: task-a + task-c`, line 8 task-b's, no markers). Assert:
- the recorded prompt or context contains 'LANDING-CONFLICT:' and e2e/shared.txt;
- at CLI start MERGE_HEAD existed and shared.txt held markers (the wrapper merged the target into W);
- the target gained exactly one more commit, with the resolved content;
- every reflog entry is still a fast-forward, local equals origin, and main is unchanged;
- seat c's session-2 finalize is 'landed' with C;
- MERGE_HEAD is gone from W afterwards;
- afterLanding passes.

Use HEAD's WT-11 spellings: the prompt prefix, MOE_WORKTREE_UNRESOLVED_CONFLICT, and how get_context serves landingRetry. Read them from the landed wrappers and fake, not from this plan.

implementationPlan.note:
