- exit 0, and no MOE_WORKTREE_UNRESOLVED_CONFLICT;
- one CLI launch, whose prompt, context or argv carries 'LANDING-CONFLICT:' and e2e/shared.txt;
- MERGE_HEAD and markers were present at CLI start;
- exactly +1 commit on the target, holding the resolved shared.txt and c.txt;
- linear() still holds;
- the c2 finalize is 'landed' on that commit;
- MERGE_HEAD is gone from W;
- afterLanding([c2]).
Trial 3 (/tmp scratch copy without the WT-13 follow assertions; not verification): c1 passed MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_CONFLICT, the unchanged target and linear(), then failed on HEAD's pre-WT-11 'rescued' finalize as expected; c2 could not run yet. The interposer's 'unlanded' and landingRetry fallback was probed directly and works. The WT-11 spellings (the prompt prefix, MOE_WORKTREE_UNRESOLVED_CONFLICT, landingRetry serving) come from the WT-11 plan and the in-flight fake; the resume session re-reads them from the landed wrapper and fake.

