implementationPlan.description:
Negative controls, then one adversarial self-review.

Negative controls: run them in scratch copies OUTSIDE the repo (copy the snapshot; never edit tracked wrappers). Each must print FAILED with the expected reason, and an unmutated control run must pass:
(i) a GATE whose probe fails (for example, create .moe in the gate cwd first, or make the gate `false && …`): parallel FAILED;
(ii) a c2 CLI that leaves the markers in place: conflict-resume FAILED (the wrapper's unresolved-conflict code, no landing);
(iii) the control left on another branch before (a): FAILED, with MOE_CONTROL_NOT_FOLLOWING seen or no landing.
Record the three results in the summary.

Self-review checklist:
- concurrency: the lease lock and attempt mirroring under two seats; atomic writes;
- no vacuous pass: every assertion has a positive counterpart, and an empty record fails;
- hermetic env: no MOE_* or session ids leak in;
- cleanup touches only the root, and only own PIDs are killed;
- no SKIP line;
- no existing file changed (`git status --short` shows only the new file);
- the request-parsing line is not embedded.

The file is test-only. Keep it at or under about 450 lines by copying only the helpers it needs. If it exceeds 400 net lines, say so and why in the summary.

Fix anything found, rerun step 5's command fresh, and submit THAT output to complete_task.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
A one-command dry run proves, on the post-WT-13 wrapper bytes and against a slash-named non-main target, that worktree mode is ready for this project's switch:
- two seats running at once land parallel tasks with fast-forward-only history;
- a conflicting task ends unlanded, then resumes via LANDING-CONFLICT and lands;
- the control checkout follows every landing;
- the candidate qualityGate passes in a .moe-free gate workspace.
It changes no existing file. The one new file supplies the per-seat isolation the single-seat shared fake lacks.

acceptanceCriteria:
DoD 2 (parallel): seats a and b, launched at once, both land on moe/work-e2e.
- exactly +2 commits, no merges, a linear first-parent history;
- every reflog entry is a fast-forward;
- local equals origin;
- main is unchanged;
- no .moe in either W.

DoD 3 (conflict-resume):
- c1: MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_CONFLICT, target unchanged, finalize_attempt 'unlanded' (conflict, path, rescue ref);
- c2: the prompt carries LANDING-CONFLICT:, MERGE_HEAD and markers are present at CLI start, the resolution lands as +1 commit;
- history stays linear and fast-forward only, and main is unchanged.

sourceAssumptions:
The fake at HEAD 204cacb8 is single-seat:
- fixed task 'task-postflight' and attempt 'attempt-postflight'/7;
- a project-wide context-count;
- a lease that grants every caller;
- finalize refuses 'unlanded' and serves no landingRetry.
Its state root is MOE_PROJECT_PATH/.moe. checkReply skips its CheckRun-before-CAS check when `git -C <project> rev-parse` fails.
